        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Georgia O'Keeffe\n- Works: Blue (O'Keeffe series)\n- Topics: Monochromatic palette, non-representational watercolor sets\n\nFacts:\n- Georgia O'Keeffe was born on November 15, 1887, and was an American artist.\n- Georgia O'Keeffe was best known for paintings of enlarged flowers, New York skyscrapers, and New Mexico landscapes.\n- Blue (O'Keeffe series) was one of Georgia O'Keeffe's watercolor sets exploring a monochromatic palette.\n- Blue (O'Keeffe series) used designs that were non-representational of specific objects.\n- Georgia O'Keeffe died on March 6, 1986.",
